            <ArticleTitle>Morbidity following isolated fractures of the sacrum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>379-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is little information in the orthopaedic literature on the long-term results following isolated fractures of the sacrum. The present study traced patients with these fractures, and attempted to identify the incidence of long-term symptoms. The study revealed that isolated fractures of the sacrum are not always benign, and may result in chronic discomfort (sacrodynia) or persistent neurological symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
